#   updates: the source of the rule is in zone trust, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind trust with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone untrust, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind untrust with --zone-network
#   ping-out: the source of the rule is in zone trust, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind trust with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone untrust, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind untrust with --zone-network; an ICMP type, or a protocol other than TCP, UDP, ICMP
#   web-in: the source of the rule is in zone untrust, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind untrust with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone dmz, and the MX names no zone: give the networks behind dmz with --zone-network
